From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (agent session)" <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 21:27:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] font: DirectWrite face with Direct2D rasterization (ADR 0005)

Adds a directwrite_harfbuzz backend: DirectWrite for face creation and
rasterization, HarfBuzz for shaping. Mirrors the existing coretext_harfbuzz
combination rather than inventing a shape - ghostty already uses a
platform-native rasterizer where one exists.

Opt-in via -Dfont-backend=directwrite_harfbuzz. The Windows default stays
freetype_windows so upstream's existing path keeps working while this
converges.

  directwrite_harfbuzz : 3065 pass, 56 skip, 0 fail
  default (freetype)   : 3065 pass, 55 skip, 0 fail  (baseline, unchanged)

The DLL imports DWrite.dll, d2d1.dll and ole32.dll, and contains no FT_*
symbols in this configuration.

Colour glyphs
-------------
Rasterization is one Direct2D path for both monochrome and colour glyphs:
TranslateColorGlyphRun returning DWRITE_E_NOCOLOR *is* the "this glyph is
monochrome" test, so there is no second rasterizer and no rule for choosing.

That call goes through IDWriteFactory4 with the full DWRITE_GLYPH_IMAGE_FORMATS
set, dispatching per glyphImageFormat to DrawColorBitmapGlyphRun /
DrawSvgGlyphRun / DrawGlyphRun - what ADR 0005 specifies and what AtlasEngine
does. IDWriteFactory2's TranslateColorGlyphRun is documented in dwrite_3.h as
"equivalent to passing TRUETYPE|CFF|COLR", so it answers NOCOLOR for any font
whose colour is not in a COLR table. Segoe UI Emoji is COLR/CPAL and works
either way, but Noto Color Emoji is CBDT/CBLC and renders only via the bitmap
path. Requesting the colour formats without TRUETYPE|CFF keeps NOCOLOR meaning
exactly "monochrome", so isColorGlyph and renderGlyph agree by construction.

Glyphs go into ghostty's CPU-side font.Atlas exactly as the FreeType face does,
rasterized once per unique glyph, so the WIC readback is not on any hot path.
This corrects a consequence stated in ADR 0005 (which claimed the atlas would
become a D2D-rendered DXGI surface); font.Atlas owns rect packing and is what
CodepointResolver/SharedGrid build on. See DESIGN.md.

A WIC bitmap render target QueryInterfaces to ID2D1DeviceContext4, so the
colour bitmap and SVG draw calls need no D3D device.

Vtable offsets
--------------
Slot indices were derived from the SDK headers and then confirmed by calling
through the raw vtable and diffing rendered pixels against the equivalent C++
virtual call - identical output, 996 opaque px. TranslateColorGlyphRun is slot
40, DrawColorBitmapGlyphRun 111, DrawSvgGlyphRun 112, GetCurrentRun 5 (the
IDWriteColorGlyphRunEnumerator1 variant, not the base one at 4). Tests assert
both the vtable size and the offset of every method actually called, and
comptime asserts pin DWRITE_COLOR_GLYPH_RUN1's layout, including the six bytes
of base tail padding MSVC does not reuse.

This also fixes an existing IDWriteFactory2 assertion that expected (3 + 5)
slots after subtracting 26, double-counting IUnknown. It had never run: the
default backend does not compile dwrite/api.zig at all.

Font metrics
------------
ex_height and cap_height come from the OS/2 table, not DWRITE_FONT_METRICS.
DirectWrite synthesizes those fields when a font omits them - a symbols-only
Nerd Font reports exactly 0.5em and ~0.7em, which look like real metrics and
are not. ghostty needs them undefined so that size adjustment falls through to
matching line height, which is what font.Collection's "adjusted sizes" test
checks. Falls back to measuring 'H' and 'x' ink when OS/2 predates version 2,
matching the FreeType backend. ic_width measures the CJK water ideograph so
the .ic_width adjustment is not silently inert.

Three things that would have been silent failures
-------------------------------------------------
name() parses the SFNT name table for real. The Windows font scanner matches
requested families against it, and only reaches FreeType's parsed family_name
when the backend has FreeType - so a placeholder would have made every font
lookup fail at runtime rather than at compile time.

HarfBuzz has no DirectWrite integration (no hb_dwrite to match hb_ft or
hb_coretext), so the font is built blob -> face -> font from the font bytes.
That required hb_font_set_scale to px*64: a blob-built font defaults to design
units, which would have put every advance out by upem/px - roughly 64x at 32px
in a 2048-upem face. Text would have drawn, just catastrophically mis-spaced.

syntheticBold/syntheticItalic copy the Face by value, so adding hb_font made
them share a handle that deinit destroys. Both now take an hb_font_reference
alongside the existing COM AddRef.

Errors reuse CannotOpenResource and CannotRenderGlyph, which already exist in
SharedGrid.RenderGlyphError - a hand-maintained union carrying its own FIXME
about consolidation, which adding Windows-specific names to would worsen.

Not yet done
------------
Discovery still uses the existing Windows font-directory scanner. DirectWrite
discovery with IDWriteFontFallback::MapCharacters and a negative cache - the
other half of ADR 0005, and the part that gives a real system fallback chain -
lands separately; GetSystemFontFallback is already bound for it. setVariations
is a no-op pending IDWriteFontFace5, so variable fonts render at their default
instance.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
